{"kind":"request","text":"LP-1: the first visible use of the live level. A member who opens a screen of a hosted room sees which other members are there now, and the entry goes away when a member leaves or the lease expires.\nThe platform part is on main and deployed (LV1 to LV5, O2). No authored package declares live presence, so no room shows it.\nStep 1, this request: a short design note, notes only, for checker review and a planner ruling. No source before the ruling.\n1. Which existing application adopts presence first, and why it is the smallest: compare Counter, Lending and Grow by the definition change, the view change and the release work each needs. The Grow recorded activity stays as it is (ruling 09c4a4cd).\n2. The exact declaration: the live definition, the presence binding of LV5 B4, the lease and the refresh, with the wake cost as requests per open view per hour and the rate for a room of five open views.\n3. The release path under the application version rule: the open version it enters, the signing, the trust row, the screen row, and the room that installs it.\n4. The witness: two real members in a browser on the hosted room, each seeing the other arrive and leave, and expiry after a closed tab.\n5. What location sharing needs beyond this (a map view, a position field, consent to share), as a list for the next request. Do not design it here.\nThis lane is the next feature after E2 and E3. The note may be written beside the gates.","body":{"conditions":"A notes-only head with checker approval; the five points answered; no source change.","target_head":"d58ff62f3980296745d652a2b0a6b7a4c6abf843","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}